 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Sure, a complementary color is one that is strongly contrasting with it, usually opposite it on color wheel. It matters because strong color contrast helps the viewer see the image clearly. If you use a calm color background, it can make the subject blur. Generally yes, though there are times when black is the strong contrast you need. It comes down to what gives the strong contrast for this particular image. Then go ahead. Just keep in mind that black can make the subject blur. Try it out on a small test piece first.",
